A BetterBash tree with this file in it has been fetched but not installed.

The fetch commands of the WebUI leave a tree in ~/.bb/bb. Nothing reads or runs
anything from that directory until it is asked to: sourcing prompt/bb.sh from
inside the tree installs the tree into ~/.bb and deletes this file, so the second
sourcing of that file only builds the prompt. Installing it later is only that:

    . ~/.bb/bb/prompt/bb.sh          # keeps the theme of this machine
    . ~/.bb/bb/prompt/bb.sh rand     # draws a new theme here

Answered the question with n? Nothing was installed and nothing will be. The tree
is a directory of files, readable, and it changes no shell until someone sources
it; a shell that starts later only mentions it, it does not install it. Running
installbb.sh of the tree directly (a script, a container) installs it too, and takes
this file away as well.

To remove a tree that was fetched and left alone:

    rm -rf ~/.bb/bb
